WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.102
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:04.504
Thank you for being here.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.272
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.907
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.909
I just want to say
to all the parents at home

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.678
eating your children's
Halloween candy,

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.246
you know what
you're doing is wrong.

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:14.580
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.850
Yeah, you can tell
today is November 1st

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.651
'cause all the Spirit Halloweens
have gone back

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:21.788
to being abandoned
Sears Outlets.

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.322
Let's get to some news.

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:26.926
Guys, the midterm elections
are just one week away.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.262
That's right. In one week,
we'll know who gets the House,

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.698
the Senate, and the upper hand
at Thanksgiving.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.265
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:33.265 --> 00:00:34.800
You can tell
the midterms are close

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.069
when the fundraising e-mails
are in all caps.

00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:39.172
"JIMMY, I NEED 10 DOLLARS NOW!"

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:41.040
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.608
And get this --
as if the midterms

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:44.811
weren't already crazy enough,
apparently the country

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:48.280
is facing
a paper-ballot shortage.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.149
Right now the MyPillow guy
is yelling at a tree

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:53.085
for rigging the election.

00:00:53.085 --> 00:00:54.754
A paper-ballot shortage.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.956
Now on Election Day,
you have to close the curtain

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.390
and just yell for
who you're voting for.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:01.594
Like, "Republican, Republican,
Democrat, Republican!"

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.463
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:05.131
Well, President Biden
is working hard

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.833
to give Democrats a final
push before the election.

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:10.869 line:0%
Starting today, he's appearing
at campaign rallies in Florida,

00:01:10.869 --> 00:01:15.007 line:0%
New Mexico, California,
Pennsylvania, and Maryland.

00:01:15.007 --> 00:01:17.477 line:0%
Yeah, if a jet-lagged
79-year-old

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:19.913
can't rally the Democrats,
nothing can.

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:22.315
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.683
[ Applause ]

00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:26.786
Yeah, today,
Biden was in Florida,

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:29.055
which is a tough place
for Democrats.

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:30.990
I mean, right now
one Democrat in Florida

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.126
is losing to an alligator
with a mullet.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:35.495
It's interesting.
Well, this is wild --

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.163 line:0%
I read that Republicans
are expecting

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.131 line:0%
former President Trump
to be indicted

00:01:39.131 --> 00:01:41.601 line:0%
soon after Election Day.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.102
Yeah, it feels like
the political version

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:44.369
of waiting to break up
with someone

00:01:44.369 --> 00:01:45.971
until after the holidays.

00:01:45.971 --> 00:01:47.974
It's like, "Ah, just..."

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:50.409
Yeah, Trump could be indicted
for the holidays,

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:54.213
which sounds kind of like
a Christmas movie on MSNBC.

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:56.415
Speaking of
the former president,

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:58.250 line:0%
Supreme Court Chief Justice
John Roberts

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.419 line:0%
just temporarily blocked
Congress

00:02:00.419 --> 00:02:04.290 line:0%
from obtaining years of Trump's
federal income tax returns.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.292
Yep, Trump was so excited,
he started chugging ketchup

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:10.163
like he'd won the Indy 500.
He's like...

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:13.232
Switching gears, now that Elon
Musk has taken over Twitter,

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:15.902
he apparently also wants
to bring back Vine

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.503
to compete with TikTok.

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:20.806
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:20.806 --> 00:02:22.141
I like it.
I think it'd be a great idea.

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:23.609
I also think it would be great
if they had a feature

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:26.011
where you could fast-forward
videos to get to the best part.

00:02:26.011 --> 00:02:27.413
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:30.149
For example,
you could skip this part...

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:31.550
Yeah.

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:34.253
And go --
go right to this part.

00:02:34.253 --> 00:02:35.488
-Ow!

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.323
-Yeah.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.359
[ Applause ]

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:43.629
